From 92e901c95ba253823dce7d604ca71044dcb5f2e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luc3as <luc3as@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 16:54:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 04/25] Quiet hours per destination, with a digest when they
 end
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A phone that buzzes at 03:14 about a jacket is a phone that mutes the bot.
A destination can now have a daily window — "23:00-07:00", crossing midnight
allowed — during which the dispatcher leaves it alone. What turns up meanwhile
is held rather than expired, its delivery clock restarts when the window ends,
and it goes out together; Telegram and Discord already fold a large batch into
one digest message, so the morning brings one summary instead of silence.

Times are read in a new TIMEZONE setting (IANA name, validated at startup).
Set with --quiet on `destination`, or per row in the dashboard, which also
gained a toggle for health notices — previously only reachable through the
CLI, which meant the "site is refusing us" warning from the last change had
nowhere to go for most people.
